CLOSING per verification 2026-09-17. The fix described in the 2026-08-06 comment is committed and on develop: commit 9f4ff6d470 ("rng: fix init_seed to match OpenMC (op-rbo)"), an ancestor of HEAD (git merge-base --is-ancestor confirms), clean git diff (no uncommitted local changes).

crates/outram-mc-libs/src/rng/lcg.rs:233-238:
  pub fn init_seed(id: i64, offset: i64, master_seed: i64) -> u64 {
      future_seed(
          (id as u64).wrapping_mul(DEFAULT_STRIDE),
          master_seed.wrapping_add(offset) as u64,
      )
  }
Exactly the two fixes the bug asked for: id now MULTIPLIES DEFAULT_STRIDE (streams a full stride apart, not one LCG step), and offset is added to master_seed (an independent run) rather than to id.
